d around the phone as he records himself while walking.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ 2. **No visible tripod or selfie stick**\n- There is **no evidence** of a tripod, monopod, or selfie stick in any frame.\n- The phone is consistently held at arm’s length or near the body — consistent with direct hand-holding, not an extended pole or mounted setup.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ 3. **Camera movement consistent with handheld operation**\n- The camera exhibits natural **jitter, slight tilts, and motion blur** (e.g., **Frame 18**, **Frame 25**) — characteristic of walking while holding a phone.\n- The framing shifts slightly as he walks and turns — **not smooth or stabilized** like a gimbal or tripod would provide.\n- In **Frame 19–24**, the camera briefly pans away from him, suggesting he turned the phone to capture the street — a maneuver only possible with direct hand control.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ 4. **No second person holding the camera**\n- In all frames where the vlogger is visible, **no other person is seen holding the camera or phone**.\n- In **Frame 1**, a man in the background is holding a phone, but he is clearly **not filming the vlogger** — he’s looking at his own screen.\n- The perspective is consistently **first-person or selfie-style**, indicating the vlogger is filming himself.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ 5. **Perspective suggesting first-person handheld recording**\n- The **angle is consistently at or near eye level**, with the vlogger’s face often centered or slightly off-center — typical of selfie-style handheld recording.\n- The **depth of field and framing** change subtly as he walks, turns, or gestures — consistent with a person actively holding and adjusting the phone while moving.\n- In **Frames 26–30**, he is clearly looking at the phone’s screen while talking and gesturing — confirming he is self-recording.\n\n---\n\n### ❗️Additional Notes:\n- The **transition from selfie mode to street view** (e.g., **Frame 19–24**) further confirms that the vlogger is manually rotating and repositioning the phone — something not possible with a fixed mount or tripod.\n- The **consistency of the camera height and angle** across frames (especially when he’s walking) supports that it’s the same person holding it — no sudden changes in perspective that would suggest a second operator or equipment change.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Final Verdict:\n**Answer ‘3’ (By hand)** is **correct**. All visual evidence across the 30 frames supports that the vlogger is directly gripping and operating the phone with his hand, with no external support or second person involved. The camera movement, framing, and physical interaction are all consistent with handheld, first-person recording.\n\n---'}, {'batch_start': 30, 'batch_end': 55, 'image_paths': ['/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/Mcggugol2ts/frames/frame_0604.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/Mcggugol2ts/frames/frame_0605.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/Mcggugol2ts/frames/frame_0606.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/Mcggugol2ts/frames/frame_0718.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/Mcggugol2ts/frames/frame_0719.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/Mcggugol2ts/frames/frame_0720.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/Mcggugol2ts/frames/frame_0721.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/Mcggugol2ts/frames/frame_0722.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/Mcggugol2ts/frames/frame_0723.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/Mcggugol2ts/frames/frame_0724.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/Mcggugol2ts/frames/frame_0725.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/Mcggugol2ts/frames/frame_0726.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/Mcggugol2ts/frames/frame_0727.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/Mcggugol2ts/frames/frame_0728.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/Mcggugol2ts/frames/frame_1479.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/Mcggugol2ts/frames/frame_1480.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/Mcggugol2t