istent with handheld operation, not a fixed mount.\n\n---\n\n✅ **4. No second person holding the camera**  \n- The vlogger is consistently alone in the frame or the only person facing the camera.  \n- No other person is visible holding or operating the camera in any frame.\n\n---\n\n✅ **5. Perspective suggesting first-person handheld recording**  \n- The framing is consistently from the vlogger’s point of view — often with his face centered or slightly off-center, looking directly into the lens.  \n- The height and angle of the camera match the natural height of someone holding a phone at arm’s length (selfie mode).  \n- The framing changes as he walks or gestures — further supporting a handheld, first-person perspective.\n\n---\n\n✅ **6. Consistent camera angle/height across shots**  \n- Across both indoor (hotel room) and outdoor (street) scenes, the camera maintains a consistent height and angle relative to the vlogger’s face — typical of someone holding the phone themselves.  \n- There’s no abrupt shift in perspective that would suggest switching between mounts or operators.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Conclusion:\nAll criteria are satisfied. The visual evidence across all 25 frames confirms that the vlogger is holding the phone **by hand** — directly gripping it, without any visible support equipment, and with movement and perspective consistent with handheld recording.\n\n**Answer: ‘3’ (By hand) is correct.**"}], 'formatted_responses': ['\n=== Batch 0-30 (30 frames) ===\nFrames: /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/Mcggugol2ts/frames/frame_0470.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/Mcggugol2ts/frames/frame_0471.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/Mcggugol2ts/frames/frame_0472.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/Mcggugol2ts/frames/frame_0473.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/Mcggugol2ts/frames/frame_0474.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/Mcggugol2ts/frames/frame_0475.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/Mcggugol2ts/frames/